Fixed N+1 queries when rendering Prefix tables — the hierarchy UI performed up to three queries per row (`children.exists`, `ancestors.count`, and the descendants count), and the available-prefix calculation performed a `descendants().exists()` per container prefix. These are now batch-resolved per page (a bounded handful of parent-chain/subtree queries) and seeded onto each row's cached properties. Also, the synthetic "available" IP-address-range rows injected into Prefix IP address tables now carry the same prefetched relations (status/role/tenant and relationship associations) as real rows instead of bypassing the table's automatic optimization. Prefix detail "Prefixes" tab: 264 → 60 queries; "Children" tab: 168 → 22; Namespace "Prefixes" tab: 136 → 54; Prefix "IP Addresses" tab: 172 → 44.
